<!--
  Full-SoLID solenoid field for the v4c yoke (compact/magnet/solenoid_v4.xml): 2D axisymmetric (r-z) map
  solenoid_SoLID_v4c_2D, solved with magnet_field/ (rzfield finite elements, open boundary, POISSON's 1010-steel
  table) on magnet_field/models/solid_v4c.am, the r-z model extracted from this geometry (octagon at its flats, spacer
  bars as rings of the same iron volume; CLEO-II coil 1282 turns x 3266 A). The copper correction coil carries
  0 A-turns: its TOSCA v4 current is not known. Replaces field_CLEOv9.xml (older CLEOv9 endcap and nose, POISSON run
  with the steel permeability frozen near mu_r = 250). Reference values (map): Bz(0,0) = 13705 G,
  Bz(0,-315 cm) = 84.3 G, Bz(0,-350 cm) = 26.7 G, |B|(r 215, z 344 cm) = 69.6 G, integral Bz dz on axis 5.260 T m
  (z -600..800 cm). 2D only: no azimuthal effects of the octagonal yoke or the discrete spacer bars.
  File: GEMC ASCII map with <mfield> header (R 0..500 cm x Z -600..800 cm, 1 cm, gauss, cylindrical-z; 30.4 MB);
  grid and unit are read from the header and cross-checked against <dimensions>. scale is dimensionless (e.g. -1 to
  flip the polarity; scaling the current this way ignores saturation).
  The map is looked up in ./fieldmaps, then in ${DETECTOR_PATH}/fieldmaps, else downloaded there once from the
  fieldmaps-v1 release of solid_dd4hep; its sha256 is checked, and an earlier download of another version is
  replaced. Offline: copy the release file into ${DETECTOR_PATH}/fieldmaps/. To regenerate it from a checkout
  (python3 with numpy, scipy and gmsh; about 2 min; magnet_field/README.md):
      magnet_field/make_maps.sh -n -f ${DETECTOR_PATH}/fieldmaps v4c
  (-n solves the committed deck after checking that the checkout's magnet files are those it was extracted
  from; without -n the deck is first re-extracted from the DD4hep geometry in the eic_xl container). A regenerated
  map has its own header comment (how and when it was made), so its sha256 differs from the release file's: to
  use it, set sha256 to the value the checksum error reports.
-->
<lccdd>
  <fields>
    <field type="SoLID_FieldMapB" name="SolenoidField" field_type="magnetic" coord_type="BrBz"
           field_map="fieldmaps/solenoid_SoLID_v4c_2D.dat"
           cache="${DETECTOR_PATH}/fieldmaps"
           url="https://github.com/JeffersonLab/solid_dd4hep/releases/download/fieldmaps-v1/solenoid_SoLID_v4c_2D.dat"
           sha256="da90b98c9faa4a4aad7776989e5781043219d63ed164e73a67a8a49431c7d54e"
           hint="Generate it from a solid_dd4hep checkout: magnet_field/make_maps.sh -n -f ${DETECTOR_PATH}/fieldmaps v4c (magnet_field/README.md)"
           scale="1.0">
      <dimensions>
        <R step="1.0*cm" min="0*cm"    max="500*cm"/>
        <Z step="1.0*cm" min="-600*cm" max="800*cm"/>
        <translationCoord x="0*cm" y="0*cm" z="0*cm"/>
      </dimensions>
    </field>
  </fields>
</lccdd>
